  "query_preview": "from eastern KS across Iowa and into the upper MS river\nvalley. Breezy NNW winds gusting 17-25 mph over central IL today.\nBroken to overcast low clouds lingered south of I-70 and from \nJacksonville sw, while much of central IL was enjoying mostly \nsunny skies. Cool temps were in the upper 40s central IL and \nlower 50s from highway 50 south. NNW winds have brought in drier\ncontinental air with dewpoints in the low to mid 30s. \n\nHigh pressure to settle over the MO valley and ridge into\ncentral IL during overnight, helping to clear skies and diminish\nwinds this evening. This will set us up for a coldest night of\nthe season and 1st widespread freeze of the season with lows \n28-32 expected. NBM has an 80-100% probability of lows below \n32F over central IL overnight north of I-70, and greater than \n50% chance southeast of I-70 getting below 32F tonight. High\nclouds to increase from the nw late tonight into Saturday as a \nweak trof approaches central IL with partly to mostly sunny\nskies and lighter winds on Saturday. Cool again with highs in\nthe lower 50s, with Lawrenceville near 55F. Another frosty\nnight expected Sat night with lows 30-35F. NBM has a 50-90% \nchance of temps getting below 32F east of I-55 overnight Sat \nnight. \n\nWest to SW winds increase on Sunday as high pressure ridge \nslips to our south/se with gusts up to 20 mph, and sunny skies,\ngiving milder highs in the lower 60s. Lows in the mid 30s Sunday\nnight. Warmup continues Monday and Tuesday with highs in the \nmid to upper 60s with a fair amount of sunshine.\n\nSemi-zonal WNW upper level flow over the Midwest during early to\nmiddle part of next week to bring fair/pleasant weather to the\narea through at least Wed. Models are trending further south\nwith a northern stream short wave into IL Wed night and Thu and\nmay bring next chance of rain showers. Though blended forecast\n(NBM) keeps pops below 15% over CWA. \n\nThe Climate Prediction Center (CPC) 8-14 Day Outlook for Nov\n13-19th has a 55-65% chance of above normal temperatures over IL\nwith precipitation trending near normal.",
